---
import DesignLayout from '../layouts/DesignLayout.astro';
---
<DesignLayout
  section="Identity"
  title="One leaf carries the decision."
  focus="How should GreenSquare AI remain recognisable across every surface?"
  description="The GreenSquare AI logo, single-leaf mark, approved colour variants and usage rules."
>
  <section class="v3-section identity-intro">
    <div class="v3-split">
      <div>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">GreenSquare AI</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="v3-lede">Four leaves establish the field. One filled leaf makes the call.</p>
        <p class="v3-note">The lower-left leaf is the fixed point of recognition. It never moves, rotates or returns to outline. The registered business name is always set as <strong>GreenSquare AI</strong> in the wordmark.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="identity-primary">
      <img src="/assets/logo-lockup-primary.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI" />
      <figcaption><span>Primary black</span><span>White mark and wordmark</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section identity-variants-section">
    <div class="identity-section-head">
      <div>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">One mark. Four controlled expressions.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Choose the treatment from the surface. Do not improvise a new colourway.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="identity-variants">
      <figure class="identity-variant identity-variant--black">
        <img src="/assets/logo-lockup-primary.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI in white on black" />
        <figcaption><strong>Primary black</strong><span>Default for covers, headers and high-authority moments.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="identity-variant identity-variant--forest">
        <img src="/assets/logo-lockup-forest.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI in lime and cream on forest" />
        <figcaption><strong>Forest</strong><span>Brand-colour alternative for owned digital surfaces.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="identity-variant identity-variant--light">
        <img src="/assets/logo-lockup-light.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI in forest and ink on white" />
        <figcaption><strong>Light</strong><span>Documents, white interfaces and print.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="identity-variant identity-variant--ink">
        <img src="/assets/logo-lockup-ink.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI in ink" />
        <figcaption><strong>Mono ink</strong><span>Single-colour production and restricted formats.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section identity-palette-section">
    <div class="identity-section-head">
      <div>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">Colour has a job before it has a name.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Use the core palette to establish GreenSquare AI. Use state colours only to carry evidence meaning. Tints support structure; they never create a second brand.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="palette-group">
      <div class="palette-group-label"><strong>Core</strong><span>Identity and authority</span></div>
      <div class="palette-swatches palette-swatches--core">
        <figure class="palette-swatch palette-swatch--black"><div></div><figcaption><strong>Black</strong><span>#10110F</span><em>Primary ground</em></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="palette-swatch palette-swatch--forest"><div></div><figcaption><strong>Forest</strong><span>#133F26</span><em>Brand field</em></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="palette-swatch palette-swatch--white"><div></div><figcaption><strong>White</strong><span>#FFFFFF</span><em>Primary surface</em></figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="palette-group">
      <div class="palette-group-label"><strong>Supporting</strong><span>Hierarchy and separation</span></div>
      <div class="palette-swatches palette-swatches--supporting">
        <figure class="palette-swatch palette-swatch--deep"><div></div><figcaption><strong>Deep</strong><span>#0B2313</span><em>Dark extension</em></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="palette-swatch palette-swatch--ground"><div></div><figcaption><strong>Ground</strong><span>#F5F5F5</span><em>Secondary surface</em></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="palette-swatch palette-swatch--line"><div></div><figcaption><strong>Line</strong><span>#DEDAD2</span><em>Rules and axes</em></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="palette-swatch palette-swatch--muted"><div></div><figcaption><strong>Muted</strong><span>#63645C</span><em>Supporting text</em></figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="palette-group palette-group--state">
      <div class="palette-group-label"><strong>Decision notation</strong><span>Small signals, never colour fields</span></div>
      <div class="state-notations" aria-label="Decision notation colours">
        <figure class="state-notation state-notation--confirmed">
          <div class="state-notation-sample" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i></div>
          <figcaption><strong>Confirmed</strong><span>#24553B</span><em>Filled marker · verified evidence</em></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="state-notation state-notation--assumption">
          <div class="state-notation-sample" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i></div>
          <figcaption><strong>Assumption</strong><span>#745B2D</span><em>Open marker · dashed test line</em></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="state-notation state-notation--uncertainty">
          <div class="state-notation-sample" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i></div>
          <figcaption><strong>Uncertainty</strong><span>#686B65</span><em>Open circle · unresolved direction</em></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="state-notation state-notation--risk">
          <div class="state-notation-sample" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i></div>
          <figcaption><strong>Material risk</strong><span>#77372F</span><em>Filled diamond · downside evidenced</em></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="palette-pairings" aria-label="Approved colour pairings">
      <div class="palette-pairing palette-pairing--black"><img src="/assets/logo-lockup-primary.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI"/><span>Primary black</span></div>
      <div class="palette-pairing palette-pairing--forest"><img src="/assets/logo-lockup-forest.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI"/><span>Owned forest</span></div>
      <div class="palette-pairing palette-pairing--light"><img src="/assets/logo-lockup-light.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI"/><span>Document white</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section identity-anatomy-section">
    <div class="v3-split identity-anatomy">
      <div class="identity-mark-stage" aria-label="GreenSquare AI single-leaf mark enlarged">
        <img src="/assets/logo-mark-white.svg" alt="" />
        <span>Fixed filled leaf</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">The filled leaf is invariant.</h2>
        <ol class="identity-rules">
          <li><div><strong>Keep it lower-left.</strong><p>Changing the filled leaf creates a different symbol.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Keep the geometry intact.</strong><p>No rotation, mirroring, stretching or redrawing.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Use supplied lockups.</strong><p>Never retype, regroup or alter “GreenSquare AI”.</p></div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Protect contrast.</strong><p>White on black, lime and cream on forest, forest and ink on light.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v3-section identity-usage-section">
    <div class="identity-section-head">
      <div>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">Lockup when naming. Mark when recognised.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The full signature introduces the organisation. The mark alone is for repeated, compact or already-labelled contexts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="identity-usage-table" role="table" aria-label="Logo use by context">
      <div class="identity-usage-row identity-usage-row--head" role="row"><span>Context</span><span>Asset</span><span>Rule</span></div>
      <div class="identity-usage-row" role="row"><strong>Website header</strong><span>Horizontal lockup</span><span>Use GreenSquare AI in full.</span></div>
      <div class="identity-usage-row" role="row"><strong>Document cover</strong><span>Primary black lockup</span><span>Preferred expression.</span></div>
      <div class="identity-usage-row" role="row"><strong>Avatar and favicon</strong><span>Mark only</span><span>White on black tile.</span></div>
      <div class="identity-usage-row" role="row"><strong>Internal interface</strong><span>Mark + live label</span><span>Only when the supplied lockup cannot fit.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="identity-minimum">Minimum width: <strong>120px</strong> horizontal lockup · <strong>20px</strong> mark only · clear space: <strong>one leaf</strong> on every side.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="v3-section identity-placement-section">
    <div class="identity-section-head">
      <div>
        <h2 class="v3-section-title-sm">Anchor the signature. Give it room.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Place the lockup on a stable edge, aligned to the content grid. The logo identifies the work; it does not float above it or compete with the conclusion.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="logo-placement-grid">
      <figure class="logo-placement logo-placement--correct">
        <div class="logo-placement-sheet"><img src="/assets/logo-lockup-light.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI"/><span>Decision brief</span><h3>Use two specialist partners.</h3></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Correct — document</strong><span>Top-left, aligned to the content grid, one-leaf clear space.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="logo-placement logo-placement--correct logo-placement--dark">
        <div class="logo-placement-sheet"><img src="/assets/logo-lockup-primary.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI"/><span>Internal decision room</span><h3>Evidence before interpretation.</h3></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Correct — dark surface</strong><span>Supplied white lockup on approved black.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="logo-placement logo-placement--incorrect">
        <div class="logo-placement-sheet"><img src="/assets/logo-lockup-light.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI"/><span>Decision brief</span><h3>Use two specialist partners.</h3></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Incorrect — floating</strong><span>Do not centre, rotate or detach the logo from the layout grid.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="logo-placement logo-placement--incorrect logo-placement--crowded">
        <div class="logo-placement-sheet"><img src="/assets/logo-lockup-light.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI"/><span>CONFIDENTIAL · DRAFT · 09 AUG</span><h3>Use two specialist partners.</h3></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Incorrect — crowded</strong><span>Do not place labels, rules or page edges inside the clear-space zone.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="logo-clearspace">
      <div class="logo-clearspace-stage">
        <span class="logo-space logo-space--top">1 leaf</span><span class="logo-space logo-space--right">1 leaf</span><span class="logo-space logo-space--bottom">1 leaf</span><span class="logo-space logo-space--left">1 leaf</span>
        <img src="/assets/logo-lockup-light.svg" alt="GreenSquare AI" />
      </div>
      <div><strong>Clear space</strong><p>Measure the exclusion zone with the width of one leaf from the mark. This is a minimum, not a target.</p></div>
      <div><strong>Preferred corners</strong><p>Top-left for covers, pages and interfaces. Bottom-left is allowed for closing frames. Use right alignment only where the whole content grid is right-anchored.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DesignLayout>
